      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. One thing my nurses struggle with is when the behavior feels very sudden or \"out of nowhere\"—like they were fine one minute and then just completely changed their demeanor, almost like they're being driven by something else entirely. It feels very chaotic. How should they manage the suddenness of those outbursts so they don't feel overwhelmed?",
